# Accepted risks — reviewed 2026-09-16.
#
# chromadb: CVE-2026-45829, CVE-2026-45830, CVE-2026-45831, CVE-2026-45833
#   All four are server-mode issues in chromadb's HTTP API: a pre-authentication
#   code injection, missing tenant/database/collection checks in
#   SimpleRBACAuthorizationProvider, and an authenticated cross-tenant
#   read/write/delete.
#   This project uses chromadb only as an embedded PersistentClient against a
#   local directory (start.py) — no HTTP server, no tenants, no auth layer, and
#   nothing but self-produced data reaches the store. None of the four is
#   reachable in this deployment.
#   There is also nothing to upgrade to: 1.5.9 is the newest release on PyPI and
#   every version is inside the affected range (no fix published upstream yet).
#   Re-check this file when chromadb ships a fix.
CVE-2026-45829
CVE-2026-45830
CVE-2026-45831
CVE-2026-45833
